regenerate.sh applies this to its copy of Mesa's
src/gfxstream/hermetic/android/gfxstream_workaround.txt, the hand-written
modules the converter appends to the root Android.bp.

aosp_mesa3d.toml builds the device drivers without virtgpu_kumquat, so the
kumquat FFI and Vulkan mapper exist only for the host test builds; link them
into mesa_platform_virtgpu only there. On Android the platform library keeps
Mesa's kumquat stub. Upstream links them everywhere, which pulls
libmagma_gpu into the device build, and that needs rustix::thread::futex,
which the ROM's rustix (libc backend, no thread feature) does not have.

--- a/gfxstream_workaround.txt
+++ b/gfxstream_workaround.txt
@@ -126,8 +126,6 @@ cc_library_static {
         "platform_virtgpu",
         "platform_virtgpu_kumquat",
         "platform_virtgpu_drm",
-        "libvirtgpu_kumquat_ffi",
-        "gfxstream_vulkan_mapper",
     ],
     static_libs: [
         "mesa_util",
@@ -143,6 +141,10 @@ cc_library_static {
     target: {
         host: {
             compile_multilib: "64",
+            whole_static_libs: [
+                "libvirtgpu_kumquat_ffi",
+                "gfxstream_vulkan_mapper",
+            ],
         },
